Z||000000||Blade||08-23-2000||12:37 PM||||Any rubbing compounds i shouldnt use?ie the plastic body. What is the best way to get back a shine?<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-23-2000||01:12 PM||||To make your Fiero Shine like glass, use Meguires 3-step Deep Crystal stuff.<BR>#1 is a paint cleaner<BR>#2 is a polish<BR>#3 is a wax<BR>The below pic is my car and it's 90% original paint!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||08-23-2000||01:32 PM||||Yep, just what Oreif said!<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18365627&Sequence=2"> <P>This is step #2 Oreif, you see the little bottle next to the buffer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">??<BR>I thought that was my car in front of my shop<BR>lol, lol, lol<P><BR>DXR_DAD<BR>**Man that black car looks GOOD!!**||||reg||13
Z||000003||Old Lar||08-23-2000||01:56 PM||||No rubbing compounds...it scrubs the clear coat off...They are too harsh.  Use the Mcguires stuff..It works great.||||reg||1
